---
/**
 * `/status` - the annunciator at full size.
 *
 * The rail is OFF here, and that is a decision rather than an omission: this page IS the
 * annunciator, and a miniature copy of it above would be a second, smaller answer to the same
 * question. ART-DIRECTION section 4.
 */
import '../styles/status.css';
import Board from '../layouts/Board.astro';
import StatusBoard from '../islands/StatusBoard.tsx';
import { API_BASE } from '../scripts/config.ts';
import type { SourceRow } from '../scripts/types.ts';

const sources: readonly SourceRow[] = [
  { claim: 'Every lamp, lit by a probe against the live database when you loaded this page', trust: 'MEASURED' },
  { claim: 'Whether the verification channel answers, as opposed to being configured', trust: 'UNKNOWN' },
];
---

<Board
  title="Status - Throughline"
  heading="What this system can actually do right now"
  description="What this system can actually do right now against the live database: vector index, embeddings and verification channel, each reported as OK, DEGRADED or UNKNOWN and never inferred."
  designator={['TLN-01 / Annunciator', 'Live probe', API_BASE]}
  sources={sources}
  colophon="The second row is not a hedge. This page does not open the verification channel to draw a lamp, because polling a third party on every page load is not a status check, so it reports configuration and says which one it is reporting."
  rail={false}
>
  <StatusBoard client:load apiBase={API_BASE} />

  <section class="prose">
    <h3>Why a lamp can be unlit</h3>
    <p>
      An unlit lamp is not an OK lamp. It means the probe could not answer, and the difference
      matters more here than anywhere else on this site: a monitor that reports a capability it
      could not measure is committing the exact failure this whole system exists to argue against.
    </p>
    <p>
      OK and DEGRADED are measurements. The vector index lamp reads OK only when the query planner
      is observed CHOOSING the index for the query recall actually runs, not when an index merely
      exists in the catalog. An index the planner ignores accelerates nothing, and reporting its
      existence as a capability would be trusting a catalog row over the system's behaviour.
    </p>
  </section>
</Board>
